editerranean Sea to the English Channel and the North Sea. Its 18 integral regions—five of which are overseas—span a combined area of 632,702 km2 (244,288 sq mi), with a total population estimated at 69.1 million in 2026. Its capital, largest city and main cultural and economic centre is Paris."}}, {"canonical_name": "Allemagne", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 11, "total_mentions": 92, "members": [{"entity_id": "allemagne", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Allemagne", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 24, "variants": ["Allemagne"], "contexts": ["northern country with scattered rocks", "country of author's return"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["country in Central Europe"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["region of various princes", "country where Tragus observed Orpine's use"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["European country"]}, {"entity_id": "german", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "German", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["German"], "contexts": ["nationality of author"]}, {"entity_id": "germany", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Germany", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 10, "variants": ["Germany"], "contexts": ["country of Herbart's associationism", "country where phosphorus debate occurred"]}, {"entity_id": "german", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "German", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory":