ific debates.", "note": "Includes references to both the country and its nationality.", "wikipedia_extract": "Germany, officially the Federal Republic of Germany, is a country in Western and Central Europe. It lies between the Baltic Sea and the North Sea to the north with the Alps to the south. Its sixteen constituent states have a total population of over 82 million, making it the most populous member state of the European Union. Germany borders Denmark to the north; Poland and the Czech Republic to the east; Austria and Switzerland to the south; and France, Luxembourg, Belgium, and the Netherlands to the west. The nation's capital and most populous city is Berlin and its main financial centre is Frankfurt; the largest urban area is the Ruhr. Settlement in the territory of modern Germany began in the Lower Paleolithic, with various tribes inhabiting it from the Neolithic onward, chiefly the Celts, and Germanic tribes inhabiting the north."}}, {"canonical_name": "Egypto", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 11, "total_mentions": 89, "members": [{"entity_id": "egypto", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Egypto", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 29, "variants": ["Egypto", "Egipto", "Egito", "Egitto", "Egjpto", "Egjrpto", "egypto"], "contexts": ["place where Cassia fistula was distributed", "country, geographical reference"]}, {"entity_id": "egypt", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Egypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Egypt"], "contexts": ["land from which Israelites were led", "ancient land of origin"]}, {"entity_id": "egyptians", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Egyptians", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Egyptians"], "contexts": ["ancient civilization"]}, {"entity_id": "ægypt", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Ægypt", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory":