ine on the Mediterranean basin, spanning thousands of islands and nine traditional geographic regions. It has a population of over 10 million. Athens is the nation's capital and largest city, followed by Thessaloniki and Patras."}}, {"canonical_name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 8, "total_mentions": 703, "members": [{"entity_id": "galen", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 478, "variants": ["Galen", "Gale", "Galem", "Galen.", "Galen. de cur. Ieteri", "Galen.inMeth. ibi", "Galeni", "Galenicos", "Galeniſtas", "Galeno", "Galenum", "Galenus", "Galenuslib", "Galia", "Galieno", "Galon"], "contexts": ["ancient medical authority", "ancient medical authority cited multiple times"]}, {"entity_id": "galen", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 18, "variants": ["Galen"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek physician and philosopher", "ancient Roman physician"]}, {"entity_id": "galens", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Galens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Galens"], "contexts": ["ancient medical authority, his library is mentioned"]}, {"entity_id": "galen", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 31, "variants": ["Dr. Galen", "Galen", "Galon"], "contexts": ["ancient Greek physician", "ancient medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "galen", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Galen"], "contexts": ["ancient medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "galen", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Galen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Galen"], "contexts": ["attests Pythagoras named Cosmos"]}, {"e