dia_extract": "Alexandria is a major city in Egypt. Lying at the western edge of the Nile River Delta, it extends about 40 km (25 mi) along the country's northern coast. It is Egypt's principal seaport, the second largest city after Cairo, and the largest city on the Mediterranean coast. Founded in 331 BC by Alexander the Great, Alexandria is one of the largest and most important cities of antiquity and a leading hub for science, culture, and scholarship. Nicknamed the \"Bride of the Mediterranean\" and \"Pearl of the Mediterranean Coast\", the city is a popular tourist destination and a major industrial centre. It is the sixth-largest city in the Arab world and in the Middle East, and the eleventh-largest city and urban area in Africa."}}, {"canonical_name": "Sapa", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 8, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "sapa", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Sapa", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 5, "variants": ["Sapa", "sapa"], "contexts": ["reduced grape must, a sweetener", "syrup of grape must, used in preparation"]}, {"entity_id": "soap", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Soap", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Soap"], "contexts": ["manufactured product"]}, {"entity_id": "sap", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "sap", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["sap"], "contexts": ["fluid circulating in plants"]}, {"entity_id": "sapos", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Sapos", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Sapos"], "contexts": ["large toads eaten by natives"]}, {"entity_id": "sap", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "sap", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants