"ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Dioscoride", "similarity": 0.86}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Dioscorides Anazarbeus", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 0.864}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Dioscoride", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Dioscoride", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Dioscoride", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Dioscorides", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Dioscoride", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dioscorides", "similarity": 0.971}], "id": 16, "stable_key": "clu_46f71b8b386d2f2f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Dioscorides", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Ancient Greek authority on materia medica and medicinal plants.", "wikipedia_extract": "Pedanius Dioscorides (Ancient Greek: Πεδάνιος Διοσκουρίδης, Pedánios Dioskourídēs; c. 40–90 AD),  \"the father of pharmacognosy\", was a Greek physician, pharmacologist, botanist, and author of De materia medica (in the original Ancient Greek: Περὶ ὕλης ἰατρικῆς, Peri hulēs iatrikēs, both meaning \"On Medical Material\"), a 5-volume Greek encyclopedic pharmacopeia on herbal medicine and related medicinal substances, that was widely read for more than 1,500 years. For almost two millennia Dioscorides was regarded as the most prominent writer on plants and plant drugs. A native of Anazarbus, Cilicia, Asia Minor, Dioscorides likely studied medicine nearby at the school in Tarsus, which had a pharmacological emphasis, and he dedicated his medical books to Laecanius Arius, a medical practitioner there. Though he writes he lived a \"soldier's life\" or \"soldier-like life\", his pharmacopeia refers almost solely to plants found in the Greek-speaking eastern Mediterranean, making it likely that he served in campaigns, or travelled in a civilian capacity, less widely than supposed. The name Pedanius is Roman, suggesting that an aristocrat of that name sponsored him to become a Roman citizen. Between 50 and 70 AD Dioscorides wrote a five-volume book in his native Greek, Περὶ ὕλης ἰατρικῆς (Perì hylēs íatrikēs), known in Western Europe more often by its Latin title De materia medica (\"On Medical Material\"), which became the precursor to all modern pharmacopeias."}}, {"canonical_name": "distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 225, "members": [{"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 168, "variants": ["distillation", "Destillat .felt.", "Distillation", "destilação", "destillada", "destilladas", "destillação", "distilação", "distillada", "distillar", "distillarem", "distillat", "distillatio", "distillatione", "distillação", "distille"], "contexts": ["implied alchemical or medicinal process", "alchemical process"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 14, "variants": ["Distillation", "Distillati∣ons", "Distilled", "distill", "distillation", "distilled"], "contexts": ["process of separating liquids", "process to obtain water"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 3, "variants": ["distillation"], "contexts": ["process of separating liquids by heating", "a process of separation by heating and cooling"]}, {"entity_id": "distilaciones", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "distilaciones", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 4, "variants": ["distilaciones", "distillation"], "contexts": ["distillation process", "used to purify principles"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 30, "variants": ["distillation", "destilação", "distilação", "distilla^ão", "distillar"], "contexts": ["process of preparing substances", "implied alchemical practice"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 5, "variants": ["Distillation", "distillation", "distillatona"], "contexts": ["practice mentioned in context of purification", "process of extracting liquids"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["distillation"], "contexts": ["process to separate alcohol from water"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "distilaciones", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "distilaciones", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "distilaciones", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "distilaciones", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "distilaciones", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "distilaciones", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 0.997}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 0.997}], "id": 17, "stable_key": "clu_ab25fdc8334e86d4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "distillation", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "A process of heating and cooling to separate or purify substances.", "wikipedia_extract": "Distillation, also classical distillation, is the process of separating the component substances of a liquid mixture of two or more chemically discrete substances; the separation process is realized by way of the selective boiling of the mixture and the condensation of the vapors in a still. Distillation can operate over a wide range of pressures from 0.14 bar (e.g., ethylbenzene/styrene) to nearly 21 bar (e.g., propylene/propane) and is capable of separating feeds with high volumetric flowrates and various components that cover a range of relative volatilities from only 1.17 (o-xylene/m-xylene) to 81.2 (water/ethylene glycol). Distillation provides a convenient and time-tested solution to separate a diversity of chemicals in a continuous manner with high purity. However, distillation has an enormous environmental footprint, resulting in the consumption of approximately 25% of all industrial energy use. The key issue is that distillation operates based on phase changes, and this separation mechanism requires vast energy inputs. Dry distillation (thermolysis and pyrolysis) is the heating of solid materials to produce gases that condense either into fluid products or into solid products."}}, {"canonical_name": "horse", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 75, "members": [{"entity_id": "horse", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "horse", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 13, "variants": ["Horse", "horse"], "contexts": ["animal with spinal stripe and leg bars", "animal used in mule hybrid"]}, {"entity_id": "horse", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Horse", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["Horse"], "contexts": ["domesticated equine", "animal that corrupts into Hornets"]}, {"entity_id": "horses", "book_id":