, "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "linnaean": "Equus caballus", "family": "Equidae", "description": "A domesticated mammal with hooves, widely used by humans.", "wikipedia_extract": "The horse (Equus ferus caballus) is a domesticated, one-toed, hoofed mammal. It belongs to the taxonomic family Equidae and is one of two extant subspecies of Equus ferus. The horse has evolved over the past 45 to 55 million years from a small multi-toed creature, Eohippus, into the large single-toed animal of today, originally in North America. Humans began domesticating horses around 4000 BCE in Central Asia, and their domestication is believed to have been widespread by 3000 BCE. Horses in the subspecies caballus are domesticated, although some domesticated populations live in the wild as feral horses. These feral populations are not true wild horses, which are horses that have never been domesticated."}}, {"canonical_name": "Firenze", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 50, "members": [{"entity_id": "firenze", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Firenze", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 27, "variants": ["Firenze", "Fiorentino", "Fiorenza", "Fiorenzi"], "contexts": ["city name", "city where the text is dated"]}, {"entity_id": "florence", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Florence", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Florence"], "contexts": ["location of observation", "city in Italy"]}, {"entity_id": "florence", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Florence", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Florence"], "contexts": ["city in Italy"]}, {"entity_id": "florence", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Florence", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Florence"], "contexts": ["city with mild winter temperature", "city with mean winter temperature"]}