um", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Papaver somniferum", "family": "Papaveraceae", "description": "Narcotic drug derived from the opium poppy, used medically and recreationally.", "wikipedia_extract": "Papaver somniferum, commonly known as the opium poppy or breadseed poppy, is a species of flowering plant in the family Papaveraceae. It is the species of plant from which both opium and poppy seeds are derived and is also a valuable ornamental plant grown in gardens. Its native range is the western Mediterranean region, but has since been obscured by widespread introduction and cultivation since ancient times to the present day. It is now naturalised across much of the world with temperate climates. Papaver somniferum is an annual herb growing to about 100 centimetres (40 inches) tall. The plant is strongly glaucous, giving a greyish-green appearance, and the stem and leaves bear a sparse distribution of coarse hairs."}}, {"canonical_name": "Naples", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 22, "members": [{"entity_id": "naples", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Naples", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 8, "variants": ["Naples"], "contexts": ["city where Don Carlos reigned", "city in Italy"]}, {"entity_id": "naples", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Naples", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Naples"], "contexts": ["city of Baptista Porta"]}, {"entity_id": "naples", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Naples", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 6, "variants": ["Naples"], "contexts": ["excursion to Naples", "location with similar latitude to New York"]}, {"entity_id": "napoles", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Napoles", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Napoles"], "contexts": ["city name", "city where Charles was"]}, {"