io_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Persia", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 23, "stable_key": "clu_a672fd7497923bfb", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Persia", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Historical and modern name for the country now known as Iran.", "wikipedia_extract": "Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and also known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west, Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest, the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast, Afghanistan to the east, Pakistan to the southeast, and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 90 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population and is the sixth-largest country in Asia. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital, largest city, and financial center. Home to one of the world's oldest continuous major civilizations, most of Iran was first united as a nation by the Medes under Cyaxares in the 7th century BC and reached its territorial height in the 6th century BC, when Cyrus the Great founded the Achaemenid Empire."}}, {"canonical_name": "Avicena", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 337, "members": [{"entity_id": "avicena", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Avicena", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 176, "variants": ["Avicena", "Avi-cena", "Avi-cenna", "AviCENA", "Avicen", "Avicenna", "Avi­­cena", "Aviçena", "Avícena"], "contexts": ["Arabian physician, known as Abolahi", "ancient medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "avicen", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Avicen", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Avicen"], "contexts": ["physician, diverged from Galen", "Persian polymath, physician, and philosopher"]}, {"entity_id": "avicenna", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name