sia.", "wikipedia_extract": "Russia, or the Russian Federation, is a country in Eastern Europe and North Asia. It is the largest country in the world, spanning eleven time zones and sharing land borders with fourteen countries. With a population of over 140 million, Russia is the most populous country in Europe and the ninth-most populous in the world. It is a highly urbanised country, with sixteen of its urban areas having more than 1 million inhabitants. Moscow, the most populous metropolitan area in Europe, is the capital and largest city of Russia, while Saint Petersburg is its second-largest city and a major cultural centre. Human settlement on the territory of modern Russia dates back to the Lower Paleolithic."}}, {"canonical_name": "Venus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 41, "members": [{"entity_id": "venus", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Venus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 16, "variants": ["venus", "Venus"], "contexts": ["sexual intercourse", "sexual activity"]}, {"entity_id": "venery", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Venery", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Venery"], "contexts": ["impotency unto Venery"]}, {"entity_id": "venery", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Venery", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 7, "variants": ["Venery", "venery"], "contexts": ["provoketh to Venery", "sexual intercourse"]}, {"entity_id": "vénus", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Vénus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Vénus"], "contexts": ["celestial body observed"]}, {"entity_id": "vénus", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Vénus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["Vénus"], "contexts": ["planet associated with inclination to scent", "title of the section"]}, {"entity_id": "transit_of_venus", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Transit of Venus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Transit of Venus"], "contexts": ["astronomical event for solar parallax", "astronomical event for parallax deduction"]}, {"entity_id": "transits_of_venus", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Transits of Venus", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Transits of Venus", "transits of Venus"], "contexts": ["observation of Venus crossing the sun", "astronomical observation"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "Venery", "similarity": 0.851}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Venery", "similarity": 0.851}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.918}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.918}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Transit of Venus", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Venus", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Transits of Venus", "similarity": 0.862}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Venery", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Venery", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Venery", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.865}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Venery", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.865}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Venery", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.865}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Venery", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 0.865}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Vénus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Vénus", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 38, "stable_key": "clu_aa9b855202dddaab", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Venus", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Relates to sexual desire, intercourse, and the planet Venus.", "note": "Can refer to the act of sex ('Venery') or the planet 'Venus'.", "wikipedia_extract": "Venus is the second planet from the Sun. It is often called Earth's \"twin\" or \"sister\" among the planets of the Solar System for its orbit being the closest to Earth's, both being terrestrial planets, and having the most similar and nearly equal size, mass, and surface gravity. Venus, though, is significantly different, especially as it has no liquid water, and its atmosphere is far thicker and denser than that of any other rocky body in the Solar System. The atmosphere is composed mostly of carbon dioxide and has a thick cloud layer of sulfuric acid that spans the whole planet. At the mean surface level, the atmosphere reaches a temperature of 737 K (464 °C; 867 °F) and a pressure 92 times greater than Earth's at sea level, turning the lowest layer of the atmosphere into a supercritical fluid. From Earth, Venus is visible as a star-like point of light, appearing brighter than any other natural point of light in the sky, and as an inferior planet it is always relatively close to the Sun, either as the brightest \"morning star\" or \"evening star\"."}}, {"canonical_name": "alembic", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 41, "members": [{"entity_id": "alembic", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "alembic", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 30, "variants": ["alembic", "Alambiques", "Allembic", "alambi", "alambicum", "alambique", "alambiques", "alembique"], "contexts": ["a distillation apparatus", "instrument for distillation"]}, {"entity_id": "alembic", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Alembic", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Alembic"], "contexts": ["distillation apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "alembics", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "alembics", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["alembics"], "contexts": ["distillation apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "alembic", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "alembic", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["alembic"], "contexts": ["implied distillation apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "alembic", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "alembic", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["alembic"], "contexts": ["implied by distillation"]}, {"entity_id": "alanbique", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "alanbique", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 1, "variants": ["alanbique"], "contexts": ["distillation apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "alambicco", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "alambicco", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "INSTRUMENT", "count": 3, "variants": ["alambicco", "alembicco", "alimbicco"], "contexts": ["apparatus for distillation", "distillation instrument"]}, {"entity_id": "alembic", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Alembic", "cate