 "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Purgatorio", "similarity": 0.826}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "purgaremse", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "purgao", "similarity": 0.881}], "id": 50, "stable_key": "clu_dbe84f442f9bc7d0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Purging", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Medical practice of cleansing the body, often with medicines.", "note": "Refers to inducing vomiting or bowel movements for medical purposes.", "wikipedia_extract": "In medicine, a cathartic is a substance that accelerates defecation. This is similar to a laxative, which is a substance that eases defecation, usually by softening feces. It is possible for a substance to be both a laxative and a cathartic. However, agents such as psyllium seed husks increase the bulk of the feces. Cathartics such as sorbitol, magnesium citrate, magnesium sulfate, or sodium sulfate were previously used as a form of gastrointestinal decontamination following poisoning via ingestion. They are no longer routinely recommended for poisonings."}}, {"canonical_name": "folhas", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 206, "members": [{"entity_id": "folhas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "folhas", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 163, "variants": ["folhas", "As fuas folhas verdes", "Favas", "falfa", "falva", "favas", "filva", "folas", "folda", "folhas da falva", "folhas da figueyraba", "folhas de Loureyro", "folhas de Sene", "folhas de acelga", "folhas de alfavaca", "folhas de arruda", "folhas de avenca", "folhas de barbaſco", "folhas de carvalho", "folhas de cerfolio", "folhas de couve", "folhas de couves", "folhas de efcabioſa", "folhas de enfayao", "folhas de enſayão", "folhas de escabiola", "folhas de eſcabioſa", "folhas de eſpinheyro alvar", "folhas de falgueyro", "folhas de falva", "folhas de falva verdes", "folhas de fenne", 