ville_1858", "target_name": "Alpine chains", "similarity": 0.873}], "id": 65, "stable_key": "clu_5189105edc204b81", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Alps", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Major European mountain range, notable for its arctic fauna and flora.", "wikipedia_extract": "The Alps () are some of the highest and most extensive mountain ranges in Europe, stretching approximately 1,200 km (750 mi) across eight Alpine countries (from west to east): Monaco, France, Switzerland, Italy, Liechtenstein, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and Hungary. The Alpine arch extends from Nice on the western Mediterranean to Trieste on the Adriatic and Vienna at the beginning of the Pannonian Basin. The mountains were formed over tens of millions of years as the African and Eurasian tectonic plates collided. Extreme shortening  caused by the event resulted in marine sedimentary rocks rising by thrusting and folding into high mountain peaks such as Mont Blanc and the Matterhorn. Mont Blanc spans the French-Italian border, and at 4,809 m (15,778 ft) is the highest mountain in the Alps. The Alpine region area contains 82 peaks higher than 4,000 m (13,000 ft)."}}, {"canonical_name": "Syria", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 34, "members": [{"entity_id": "syria", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Syria", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 24, "variants": ["Syria", "Siria", "Siría", "Syría", "Síria"], "contexts": ["region where cubebs were questioned", "region where 'Musa' was used"]}, {"entity_id": "syria", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Syria", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 6, "variants": ["Syria"], "contexts": ["country with a popular belief about aërolites", "country, center of earthquake circle"]}, {"entity_id": "siria", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Siria", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Siria"], "contexts": ["land where mineral is found"]}, {"entity_id": "syria", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Syria", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Syria"], "contexts": ["coast with different marine plants"]}, {"entity_id": "assyrian", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Assyrian", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 2, "variants": ["Assyrian"], "contexts": ["ancient civilization known for architecture", "ancient civilization"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Syria", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Syria", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Syria", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Siria", "similarity": 0.968}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Syria", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Syria", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Syria", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Siria", "similarity": 0.968}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Syria", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Syria", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Siria", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Syria", "similarity": 0.968}], "id": 66, "stable_key": "clu_b7c5d834400f7768", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Syria", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A region in the Middle East.", "wikipedia_extract": "Syria, officially the Syrian Arab Republic, is a country in West Asia located in the Eastern Mediterranean and the Levant. It borders the Mediterranean Sea to the west, Turkey to the north and northwest, Iraq to the east and southeast, Jordan to the south, and Israel and Lebanon to the southwest. It is a republic under a provisional government and comprises 14 governorates. Damascus is the capital and largest city. With a population of 26 million across an area of 185,180 square kilometres (71,500 sq mi), it is the 56th-most populous and 87th-largest country. The name \"Syria\" historically referred to a wider region."}}, {"canonical_name": "frog", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "frog", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "frog", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 19, "variants": ["Frog", "FROG", "frog"], "contexts": ["animal used for nerve-centre study", "living animal used in experiment"]}, {"entity_id": "frogs", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Frogs", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Frogs"], "contexts": ["oviparous quadruped with analogous joints"]}, {"entity_id": "frogs", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Frogs", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "AMPHIBIAN", "count": 3, "variants": ["Frogs", "frogs"], "contexts": ["amphibian species", "animals that cannot cross wide ocean spaces"]}, {"entity_id": "frogs", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "frogs", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "REPTILE", "count": 6, "variants": ["frogs"], "contexts": ["creatures for vivisection study", "animal studied for reflex movements"]}, {"entity_id": "frog", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "frog", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "AMPHIBIAN", "count": 1, "variants": ["frog"], "contexts": ["animal whose blood contains animalcules"]}, {"entity_id": "frog", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "frog", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["frog"], "contexts": ["limbs of a dead 