ce, a 1907 novel by Rose Macaulay \"The Furnace\" (short story), by Stephen King HMS Furnace, four ships of the Royal Navy Walt Furnace (born 1943), American businessman and politician"}}, {"canonical_name": "Headach", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 28, "members": [{"entity_id": "headach", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Headach", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 24, "variants": ["Headach", "Head-ach", "Headaches"], "contexts": ["pain in the head", "symptom of brain diseases"]}, {"entity_id": "headach", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "headach", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["headach"], "contexts": ["pain in the head treated with Loadstone"]}, {"entity_id": "headaches", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "headaches", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["headaches"], "contexts": ["pain in the head"]}, {"entity_id": "headaches", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "headaches", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["headaches"], "contexts": ["symptom of illness"]}, {"entity_id": "headache", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "headache", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["headache"], "contexts": ["pain in the head"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Headach", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "headach", "similarity": 0.992}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Headach", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "headaches", "similarity": 0.969}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Headach", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "headaches", "similarity": 0.969}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Headach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "headache", "similarity": 0.975}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "headach", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "headaches", "similarity": 0.978}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "headach", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "headaches", "similarity": 0.978}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "headach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "headache", "similarity": 0.982}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "headaches", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "headaches", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "headaches", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "headache", "similarity": 0.981}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "headaches", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "headache", "similarity": 0.981}], "id": 69, "stable_key": "clu_73257aec0c126571", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Headache", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A common symptom characterized by pain in the head.", "wikipedia_extract": "A headache, also known as cephalalgia, is the symptom of pain in the face, head, or neck. It can occur as a migraine, tension-type headache, or cluster headache. There is an increased risk of depression in those with severe headaches. Headaches can occur as a result of many conditions. There are a number of different classification systems for headaches. The most well-recognized is that of the International Headache Society, which classifies it into more than 150 types of primary and secondary headaches."}}, {"canonical_name": "mace", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "mace", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "mace", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 16, "variants": ["mace", "Macc", "Mace"], "contexts": ["fragrant spice for pounding", "aril of nutmeg, a spice"]}, {"entity_id": "mace", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Mace", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mace"], "contexts": ["flosculous coat of nutmeg fruit"]}, {"entity_id": "mace", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Mace", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Mace"], "contexts": ["spice from nutmeg", "spice added to decoctions"]}, {"entity_id": "ma", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Ma", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Ma"], "contexts": ["plant genus, possible misidentification", "tree with large leathery leaves"]}, {"entity_id": "mayz", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Mayz", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Mayz"], "contexts": ["leaves fed to fatten worms", "grain, nutritious and healthy"]}, {"entity_id": "macedonica", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "macedonica", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["macedonica", "Macedonico"], "contexts": ["spice, likely mace", "spice, mace"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "mace", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "Mace", "similarity": 0.928}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "mace", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Ma", "similarity": 0.828}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "mace", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Mayz", "similarity": 0.845}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Mace", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Mace", "similarity": 0.907}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Mace", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Ma", "similarity": 0.832}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Mace", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "macedonica", "similarity": 0.821}], "id": 70, "stable_key": "clu_6804b87751aca508", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "mace", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Myristica fragrans", "family": "Myristicaceae", "description": "Spice from the aril of the nutmeg fruit.", "note": "Contexts for 'Ma' and 'Mayz' suggest possible confusion with maize (corn).", "wikipedia_extract": "Myristica fragrans, commonly known as the nutmeg tree, is an evergreen species indigenous to the Maluku Islands of Indonesia. This aromatic tree is economically significant as the primary source of two distinct spices: nutmeg, derived from its seed, and mace, obtained from the seed's aril. Valued for centuries in global spice trade, M. fragrans is now widely cultivated throughout tropical regions, including parts of Southeast Asia (Indonesia, Malaysia), South Asia (Kerala in India, Sri Lanka), East Asia (Guangdong and Yunnan in China, Taiwan), the Caribbean (notably Grenada), and South America. Myristica fragrans is an evergreen tree, usually 5–15 m (16–49 ft) tall, but occasionally reaching 20 m (66 ft) or even 30 m (98 ft) on Tidore. The alternately arranged leaves are dark green, 5–15 cm (2.0–5.9 in) long by 2–7 cm (0.8–2.8 in) wide with petioles about 1 cm (0.4 in) long. The species is dioecious, i.e. \"male\" or staminate flowers and \"female\" or carpellate flowers are borne on different plants, although occasional individuals produce both kinds of flower."}}, {"canonical_name": "Irlande", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "irlande", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Irlande", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 12, "variants": ["Irlande"], "contexts": ["Country", "country with a higher relative population"]}, {"entity_id": "ireland", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Ireland", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ireland"], "contexts": ["shore location for compass variation"]}, {"entity_id": "iseland", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Iseland", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Iseland"], "contexts": ["Country from which stones are brought"]}, {"entity_id": "ireland", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Ireland", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Ireland"], "contexts": ["Ireland has few animals", "island for distance comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "ireland", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ireland", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Ireland"], "contexts": ["country where Belfast is located", "shores receive tropical seeds"]}, {"entity_id": "ireland", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Ireland", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Ireland"], "contexts": ["location of base measurement", "island with western coasts"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Irlande", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Irlande", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "Iseland", "similarity": 0.841}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Irlande", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Irlande", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Irlande", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 0.971}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Ireland", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ireland", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 71, "stable_key": "clu_02d20d62d6315c04", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ireland", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "An island country with a notable population density.", "wikipedia_extract": "Ireland is an island in the North Atlantic Ocean, in Northwestern Europe. Geopolitically, the island is divided between the Republic of Ireland (officially named Ireland – a sovereign state covering five-sixths of the island) and Northern Ireland (part of the United Kingdom – covering the remaining sixth). It is separated from Great Britain to its east by the North Channel, the Irish Sea, and St George's Channel. Ireland is the second-largest island of the British Isles, the third-largest in Europe, and the twentieth-largest in the world. As of 2022, the population of the entire island is just over 7 million, with 5.1 million in the Republic of Ireland and 1.9 million in Northern Ireland, ranking it the second-most populous island in Europe after Great Britain. The geography of Ireland comprises relatively low-lying mountains surrounding a central plain, with several navigable rivers extending inland."}}, {"canonical_name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "ganges", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 14, "variants": ["Ganges"], "contexts": ["river in India", "valley in India"]}, {"entity_id": "ganges", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 5, "variants": ["Ganges", "Gange"], "contexts": ["river", "river in India"]}, {"entity_id": "ganges", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Ganges"], "contexts": ["river in India", "major river in India"]}, {"entity_id": "ganges", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ganges"], "contexts": ["river in India"]}, {"entity_id": "ganges", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Ganges", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Ganges"], "contexts": ["river with mouths causing bore", "river with tidal wave at mouths"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Ganges", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ganges", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 72, "stable_key": "clu_2884614e5d3dcc2c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ganges River", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Major river in India, important geographical and historical feature.", "wikipedia_extract": "The Ganges ( GAN-jeez; in India: Ganga,  GUNG-ah; in Bangladesh: Padma,  PUD-mə) is a trans-boundary river of Asia which flows through India and Bangladesh. The 2,525-kilometre-long (1,569 mi) river rises in the western Himalayas in the Indian state of Uttarakhand. It flows south and east through the Gangetic plain of North India, receiving the right-bank tributary, the Yamuna, which also rises in the western Indian Himalayas, and several left-bank tributaries from Nepal that account for the bulk of its flow. In West Bengal, India, a feeder canal taking off from its right bank diverts 50% of its flow southwards, artificially connecting it to the Hooghly River. The Ganges continues into Bangladesh, its name changing to the Padma. It is then joined by the Jamuna, the lower stream of the Brahmaputra, and eventually the Meghna, forming the major estuary of the Ganges Delta, and emptying into the Bay of Bengal."}}, {"canonical_name": "oliveira", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 20, "members": [{"entity_id": "oliveira", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "oliveira", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 10, "variants": ["oliveira", "olivastro", "oliveiras"], "contexts": ["tree size comparison", "tree comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "oyl_olive", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Oyl Olive", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Oyl Olive"], "contexts": ["oil used in Costmary salve", "oil from ripe olives, temperate quality"]}, {"entity_id": "olives", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Olives", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Olives"], "contexts": ["unripe fruit used for oil"]}, {"entity_id": "olivier", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "olivier", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["olivier"], "contexts": ["tree compared to coconut tree"]}, {"entity_id": "oliveyra", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "oliveyra", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "PLANT", "count": 5, "variants": ["oliveyra", "Oliveyra", "olivera"], "contexts": ["signer of document", "author of the text"]}, {"entity_id": "olive", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "olive", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["olive"], "contexts": ["Mediterranean tree bearing olives"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "oliveira", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Oyl Olive", "similarity": 0.871}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "oliveira", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Olives", "similarity": 0.902}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "oliveira", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "olivier", "similarity": 0.856}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "oliveira", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "oliveyra", "similarity": 0.977}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "oliveira", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "olive", "similarity": 0.899}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Oyl Olive", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "oliveyra", "similarity": 0.878}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Oyl Olive", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "olive", "similarity": 0.842}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Olives", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "oliveyra", "similarity": 0.893}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Olives", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "olive", "similarity": 0.865}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "olivier", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "oliveyra", "similarity": 0.837}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "olivier", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "olive", "similarity": 0.896}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "oliveyra", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "olive", "similarity": 0.887}], "id": 73, "stable_key": "clu_ba9a422b09fc36f4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "olive tree", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Olea europaea", "family": "Oleaceae", "description": "Tree producing olives and olive oil, valued for its fruit and oil.", "wikipedia_extract": "The olive (botanical name Olea europaea, \"European olive\") is a species of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Originating in Asia Minor, it is abundant throughout the Mediterranean Basin, with wild subspecies in Africa and western Asia; modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. The olive is the type species for its genus, Olea, and lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family, which includes lilac, jasmine, forsythia, and ash. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil—now used to describe any viscous water-insoluble liquid—was originally synonymous with olive oil, the liquid fat derived from olives. The olive has deep historical, economic, and cultural significance in the Mediterranean."}}, {"canonical_name": "Nil", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 19, "members": [{"entity_id": "nil", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Nil", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 7, "variants": ["Nil"], "contexts": ["river in Africa", "river from which Egyptians did not come"]}, {"entity_id": "nilus", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Nilus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Nilus"], "contexts": ["river Nile"]}, {"entity_id": "nile", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Nile", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 4, "variants": ["Nile"], "contexts": ["river where Bichir is found", "river with associated granit blocks"]}, {"entity_id": "nilo", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Nilo", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 4, "variants": ["Nilo"], "contexts": ["river associated with Alexandria", "river near the cinnamon region"]}, {"entity_id": "nilo", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Nilo", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Nilo"], "contexts": ["river", "river whose water was considered pure"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Nil", "target_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "target_name": "Nilus", "similarity": 0.929}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Nil", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Nile", "similarity": 0.946}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Nil", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.899}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Nil", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.899}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nilus", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Nile", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nilus", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.918}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Nilus", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.918}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Nile", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.931}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Nile", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 0.931}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Nilo", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Nilo", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 74, "stable_key": "clu_32d9aec44ab246b9", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Nile River", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "The major river of northeastern Africa, historically significant.", "wikipedia_extract": "The Nile River is a major north-flowing river in northeastern Africa which flows into the Mediterranean Sea. At 7,088 km (4,404 mi) long, it is the longest river in the world, although the volume of water it carries is much smaller than other major rivers such as the Amazon or Congo. Its drainage basin covers portions of eleven countries: the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Tanzania, Burundi, Rwanda, Uganda, Kenya, Ethiopia, Eritrea, South Sudan, Sudan, and Egypt. It plays an important economic role in the economy of these nations, and it is the primary water source for South Sudan, Sudan and Egypt. The Nile has two major tributaries: the White Nile and the Blue Nile. The White Nile, being longer, is considered to be the headwaters, although the Blue Nile contributes 80% of the water and silt below the confluence of the two."}}, {"canonical_name": "Scorpio", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 18, "members": [{"entity_id": "scorpio", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Scorpio", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 6, "variants": ["Scorpio"], "contexts": ["constellation with starless patches", "constellation in zodiac"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpions", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Scorpions", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Scorpions"], "contexts": ["creatures of higher mischiefs", "arachnids producing higher mischiefs"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpion", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Scorpion", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Scorpion"], "contexts": ["Animal whose sting is treated"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpions", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Scorpions", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Scorpions", "Scorpiions"], "contexts": ["venomous creature", "arachnid known for venom"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpioni", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Scorpioni", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Scorpioni"], "contexts": ["scorpions used in preparation"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpion", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "scorpion", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "ANIMAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["scorpion", "scorpi"], "contexts": ["venomous creature", "used in wound treatment"]}, {"entity_id": "escorpiao", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Escorpiao", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Escorpiao"], "contexts": ["venomous scorpion"]}, {"entity_id": "scorpiomortiferum", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Scorpiomortiferum", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Scorpiomortiferum"], "contexts": ["dead scorpion"]}, {"entity_id": "ξ_scorpio", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "ξ Scorpio", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["ξ Scorpio"], "contexts": ["star system that is triple"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Scorpio", "target_book": "pseudod